<div id="2026-09-02-hdry-import-and-queue" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-02 — imported 12 missing HDRY parts + queued door hardware and wheel parts</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Created 12 <code>printing_3d_models</code> rows for parts that existed on disk but were never imported, then queued 9 of them. Queue went 22 jobs &rarr; <b>31 jobs / 66 units</b>, still zero duplicates.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>User decisions applied.</strong> (1) one wheel = 2 half-wheels + 1 tire, so 4 wheels = 8 halves + 4 tires; (2) wheel support foot = 4, one per wheel; (3) <code>Wheel_M.stl</code> left unidentified; (4) FFL01 &mdash; import BOTH sensor and no-sensor variants, sensor default because a drying cabinet implies an AMS/multi-colour printer (user runs a Kobra 3 with AMS, plans a K2).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Imported (12).</strong> Door hardware: female hinge L/R, male hinge L/R, hinge latch L/R, door handle, window shape. Wheel kit: support foot (<code>Foot__1___1_.stl</code>, 292 cm&sup3;), tire (<code>Gomma.stl</code>, 85 cm&sup3;). Plus <code>Wheel_M.stl</code> (unidentified variant) and <code>FFL01_Sensor.stl</code>. <code>FFL01_no_Sensor</code> was already model 38, so it was skipped rather than duplicated.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Queued (9).</strong> #93&ndash;99 door hardware (q1 each), #100 wheel support foot (q4), #101 wheel tire (q4). The unidentified <code>Wheel_M</code> variant was deliberately NOT queued.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>On Wheel_M.</strong> Tested whether it is a mirror of <code>Wheel.stl</code>: mirror-X halves the chamfer distance (3.33 &rarr; 1.70) but 1.70 is far above the ~0.2 identical threshold, and it is <b>3 mm thicker</b> (17.1 vs 14.1 mm). It is a genuinely different part, not a mirrored half. Imported but flagged <code>UNIDENTIFIED</code> with no BOM line and no queue entry pending identification.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why the wheel kit had no support.</strong> Its BOM (item 99) listed only hardware &mdash; bolt/nut, spacer, washer &mdash; with no printed sub-lines. The printed foot and tire were never captured, so the kit could never be complete. The imported foot/tire are now queued, but <b>the kit BOM itself still has no printed lines</b> &mdash; adding them is Inventory-domain and needs the kit BOM corrected.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> New <code>script/hdry_import_candidates.pl</code> and <code>script/hdry_queue_missing.pl</code> (both idempotent, dry-run default, geometry-gated). Worksheet at <code>/Documentation/hdry_parts_worksheet</code>; generator <code>hdry_work/worksheet_data.py</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Still open.</strong> Wheel_M identity; kit BOM printed lines; FLS02 has no STL at all; three wrongly-printed parts (#58 BBR01, #61 BR01, #63 FL01) still need reprinting; desiccant box has no live job.</p>
</div>
